    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p19_b36",
      "text": "The formal inequality still contains the unknown log-moment term under \u03c00, but its three\nterms explain why KL drift is a sensible observable proxy for reward uncertainty. The\nleft-hand side is an analogue of the promptwise \u21131 error between the proxy reward and\nthe certainty-equivalent true reward; the log-moment term can be treated as a baseline\nconstant because it is evaluated under the fixed reference policy rather than the current\npolicy; and the KL term is the observable policy-drift statistic that remains, with the\n",
      "bbox": [
        71.58,
        521.07,
        523.62,
        622.67
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
